[b][size=5]Quickslot[/size][/b]

Equipment and consumable shortcut groups with a configurable HUD. Tap a group key to equip or use its remembered entry. Hold, browse and release to select another.

[b]Features[/b]
[list]
[*]Up to eight groups for weapons, armor, shields, spells, scrolls, potions, poisons, food, powers, shouts and ammo.
[*]Searchable hand combinations, including smart weapons and shields.
[*]Armor, clothing and jewelry in any group: a tap puts a piece on and the next tap takes it off.
[*]Outfits: one tap wears a saved set of pieces, with or without both hands, and a tap on a worn outfit puts back what you wore before.
[*]Groups populated automatically from one or more Skyrim Favorites categories.
[*]Hand buttons while the selector is open: mouse buttons or triggers put an item in either hand or take it out, and the hand is remembered. Per-group [b]Hand[/b] policy chooses Per item, Always right or Always left.
[*]Smart weapons by physical damage, shields by armor, ammo by damage and potions by strength or best fit.
[*]A Tap choice for each group, equip the last item or step to the next, with optional hold-to-browse.
[*]Spell casting without equipping: a quick-cast group casts its selected spell on a tap, and an Oblivion-style group readies a spell for a Cast key. Needs Open Animation Replacer and Quickslot Casting Animations.
[*]New characters start with groups that follow their Skyrim Favorites.
[*]A dedicated consumable binding for using the last selected potion, food or poison.
[*]Keyboard, XInput, PS4 and experimental VR controls with configurable modifiers.
[*]Independent equipment display with Grid and Free layouts, right-edge mirroring, per-role visibility, quantity badges, poison indicators, bow ammunition counts, shout timers and power dimming.
[*]Separate keyboard/mouse and controller options for using Quickslot while QuickLoot is open.
[*]Cards, squares, circles, diamonds, hexagons, frameless icons, unified hotbars, a compact scrollable list selector and a wheel selector with tile or segmented-ring styles.
[*]Independent Size (25%–300%), Text size (50%–300%), opacity and anchored placement for the widget, selector and equipment display, plus Peek HUD live preview mode.
[*]A wheel you can shape: size, ring thickness, gaps, highlight styles, raised pointed segments, rotation, and an optional center circle.
[*]Full item stats and effect descriptions while browsing, plus enchantment charge as diamonds under the weapon's name and on its icon as a color fill or a small soul gem.
[*]16 bundled 2.5D PBR theme packs with automatic UI detection and live reload, icon sets, custom colors, per-group colors and an equipped-item highlight.
[*]A preset manager with built-in layouts (including Souls Cross and Action Bar), automatic presets for controller and keyboard, Undo, automatic saving and menu translations.
[/list]

[b]Requirements[/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library[/url] matching your game executable.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/12604]SkyUI[/url] and Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable, x64.
[*]VR: SKSEVR, [url=https://github.com/alandtse/skyrim_vr_address_library]VR Address Library[/url], [url=https://github.com/Odie/skyui-vr]SkyUI VR[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/183466]ImGui VR Helper 1.9.4+[/url].
[/list]

Spell casting: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/92109]Open Animation Replacer[/url] 3 or later and Quickslot Casting Animations, the second file on this page.

Optional integrations: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/85702]Inventory Interface Information Injector (I4) 1.1.0+[/url] for item artwork (without it, items show SkyUI category icons), [url=https://github.com/rijosan87/PNGII]PNG Icon Injector[/url] with icon API v1, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/120352]SKSE Menu Framework[/url], ImGui Icons and Skyrim Souls RE.

[b]Controls[/b]

Open the editor with [b]Shift + \[/b]. Add items in Groups; New creates combinations, outfits and smart shortcuts. Changes save automatically.

Hold a group key and use the wheel or Left/Right to browse. Release to select. Ctrl + Left/Right reorders; both actions wrap. In Inventory and Magic, Ctrl + a group key adds the highlighted item for the right hand and Ctrl + Shift adds it for the left. During gameplay a group key held with Ctrl, Shift or Alt selects the group; enable Controls → Keyboard → Use editing shortcuts during gameplay to add the equipped right or left hand with Ctrl or Ctrl + Shift, unequip with Shift and remove a shortcut with Alt. While browsing, Backspace unequips and Delete removes the highlighted shortcut.

On controller, groups use D-pad directions by default. Hold a group button and browse with the right stick or LB/RB. Release to select, B/Circle to cancel, X/Square to unequip. Hold D-pad Up and press Start/Options to open the editor. The editor supports D-pad focus, right-stick pointer, click/drag and on-screen text entry.

Configure bindings under Controls. Keyboard actions use None or Clear to disable a binding. For Alt-to-walk setups, assign Remove group shortcut to another modifier or None and enable Allow group selection with unused modifiers.

While the selector is open, the left mouse button or RT puts the highlighted item in the right hand and the right mouse button or LT in the left. Pressing the button of the hand an item is already in takes it out. Settings from earlier versions adopt these bindings with Use mouse buttons for hands and Use triggers for hands.

With [b]Tap → Step to the next item[/b], the first tap when returning to a group recalls the selected item and further taps advance. [b]Hold to browse[/b] opens the selector when the key is held. [b]Keep the other hand equipped while cycling[/b], under Controls → General, starts enabled and skips weapon copies held in the opposite hand.

Groups that equip their last item use a consumable on a tap. Set [b]Consumables → Use selected consumable action[/b], or choose Step to the next item, to select consumables with the group key and consume one dose with a separate binding. Bind [b]Use selected consumable[/b] under Controls → Keyboard or Controller. The action starts unbound and uses the last explicitly selected consumable across groups; the equipment display shows that selection.

In Groups, open the Manual dropdown and check the Favorites categories to include. For example, combine Favorite weapons with Favorite shields / torches. The group displays matching favorites once each, in alphabetical order.

[b]Appearance[/b]

Built-in themes include Minimal and Skyrim silver, alongside 16 bundled 2.5D PBR theme packs: interface-matching packs for Amethyst, Dear Diary Dark, Edge, Horizons, Immortal, Norden, Nordic, Oathvein, Outlander, Untarnished and Vel'dun, plus standalone Crimson Filigree, Daedric Oblivion, Dwemer Aetherium, Imperial Parchment and Sovngarde Astral themes. Appearance has a page each for Theme, Widget, Selector, Equipment and General, with [b]Peek HUD[/b] to dock the editor as a side-drawer over the live HUD. Every slider has step buttons and a reset; Reset page and Reset all appearance restore the defaults.

Each display holds on to one of nine screen anchors with a pixel offset. The Free arrangement places and sizes each group's tile or equipment cell on its own, with Align, Distribute and snap guides in Position mode. Drag or resize a display, nudge it with the arrow keys or LB + D-pad, or center it. Screen area keeps the HUD inside a 16:9, 2:1 or 21:9 area on ultrawide screens.

Presets lists built-in Default, Cards, Cross, Diamond, Circle, Wheel, Souls Cross and Action Bar layouts above your own. New installations show diamond tiles with an arc selector. Rename, duplicate, update and delete presets, preview them, and apply their look, controls or groups. Input device presets switch the look when you change between controller and keyboard.

[b]Equipped highlight[/b] under Appearance → Theme outlines or tints the tile of an equipped item. [b]Wheel style → Segments[/b] under Appearance → Selector turns the wheel into a ring of wedges with the pointed item's name in the center; the Wheel section sets its ring thickness, gaps, highlight, raised pointed segments, rotation and center circle. [b]Selector → Style → List[/b] opens a compact scrollable panel with inline hand, equipped, poison, quantity and cooldown indicators.

Under [b]Appearance → Theme → Icons → Item icons[/b], choose [b]I4[/b] (your installed I4 packs, then SkyUI), [b]SkyUI[/b] (SkyUI category icons), or [b]PNGII[/b] (PNG Icon Injector artwork, then I4, then SkyUI). Original displays artwork colors; Theme and White apply the selected tint. Smart shortcuts show the item currently selected, combinations show both items, and hand actions use a gauntlet.

The equipment display shows the right hand, left hand, ammunition, selected consumable, power/shout and ready spell, with Grid and Free layouts, right-edge mirroring and per-role visibility. Quantities and shout timers appear on icons. Groups and equipment have independent visibility settings, including [b]Keep visible in combat[/b] and [b]Keep visible with weapons drawn[/b].

Settings holds language, interface sounds, input device presets, QuickLoot input, the character option and Reset Quickslot, which returns to a new installation's settings and Favorites groups. Appearance pages start with their main settings; Show advanced settings adds the rest.

[b]Downloads and support[/b]

[url=https://github.com/opteron-x86/quickslot-hotkeys]Source and documentation[/url] · [url=https://github.com/opteron-x86/quickslot-hotkeys/releases]Releases[/url]

The DLL targets SE 1.5.97, AE 1.6.x, 1.7.99/1.7.104 and VR 1.4.15. VR support is experimental.

For bug reports, include Quickslot.log, the game version and reproduction steps. Include a crash log for crashes.

[b]Credits[/b]

Item artwork comes from your installed I4 and PNGII packs. Frame/font attribution and dependency notices are in the [url=https://github.com/opteron-x86/quickslot-hotkeys/tree/master/licenses]licenses folder on GitHub[/url].
